From: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: clock the IPQ5332 PPE at the vendor rate

qcom_ppe_probe() sets a PPE clock rate of 353 MHz, the IPQ9574 rate, for
every SoC.  ppe_clock_init_and_reset() requests it for the PPE clocks and
derives the NSSNOC PPE interconnect votes from it, and
edma_clock_configure() requests it for the EDMA clocks.  On IPQ5332 the
PPE clock source offers 200 MHz and 300 MHz, so the PPE, EDMA and port
MAC clocks, which all derive from nss_cc_ppe_clk_src, run at 300 MHz.

The IPQ5332 CMN PLL has a dedicated 200 MHz PPE output
(IPQ5332_PPE_200MHZ_CLK), and the vendor SSDK clocks the IPQ5332 PPE
(MPPE, revision 1 of the IPQ9574 APPE) at MPPE_CLK_RATE, 200 MHz,
against APPE_CLK_RATE, 353 MHz, for the IPQ9574 (include/init/ssdk_clk.h
and ssdk_appe_fixed_clock_init() in qca-ssdk), and sets the NSSNOC PPE
clocks to the same rate.  The same driver programs the MPPE scheduler
tables and buffer budgets that this driver uses for IPQ5332.

Request 200 MHz on IPQ5332 so that the PPE runs at the vendor rate and
the interconnect votes follow it.  With the previous patch the
mitigation timers keep their programmed durations across the change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: François Guerraz <kubrick@fgv6.net>
---
Not measured on hardware yet.  The stock firmware rate is taken from the
public qca-ssdk source (win_qsdk.common.1.10.r2), not read back from a
running stock unit.

In OpenWrt this overrides the 300 MHz entry that the IPQ53xx subtarget
series adds to the IPQ5332 NSSCC PPE frequency table.  Dropping this
patch restores 300 MHz for comparison.
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe.c
@@ -23,6 +23,11 @@
 #define PPE_PORT_MAX		8
 #define PPE_CLK_RATE		353000000
 
+/* The IPQ5332 CMN PLL has a dedicated 200 MHz PPE output, and the vendor
+ * SSDK clocks the IPQ5332 (MPPE) PPE, EDMA and port MACs at that rate.
+ */
+#define PPE_CLK_RATE_IPQ5332	200000000
+
 /* ICC clocks for enabling PPE device. The avg_bw and peak_bw with value 0
  * will be updated by the clock rate of PPE.
  */
@@ -229,7 +234,8 @@ static int qcom_ppe_probe(struct platfor
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, PTR_ERR(ppe_dev->regmap),
 				     "PPE initialize regmap failed\n");
 	ppe_dev->dev = dev;
-	ppe_dev->clk_rate = PPE_CLK_RATE;
+	ppe_dev->clk_rate = ppe_is_ipq5332(ppe_dev) ? PPE_CLK_RATE_IPQ5332 :
+			    PPE_CLK_RATE;
 	ppe_dev->num_ports = num_ports;
 	ppe_dev->num_icc_paths = num_icc;
 
